# Build Iris-Main With CocoaPods

`VideoLab` is integrated through CocoaPods, so CLI builds must use the generated workspace, not the Xcode project.

Use this command for a compile-only simulator build:

```bash
cd "/Users/abdur-rahmanrana/Documents/Magnolia Creative/Dev/Iris-Main"
xcodebuild build \
  -workspace "Iris-Main.xcworkspace" \
  -scheme "Iris-Main" \
  -configuration Debug \
  -destination "generic/platform=iOS Simulator" \
  CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
```

Do not build with `-project "Iris-Main.xcodeproj"` for normal verification. That bypasses CocoaPods integration and can fail with `no such module 'VideoLab'`.
